{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kemenyConstant","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vol · (Σᵢ πᵢ (L_g⁻¹)ᵢᵢ − πᵀ L_g⁻¹ π), π the stationary distribution, which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(1\/2vol) Σᵢⱼ dᵢ dⱼ R(i, j) (commute times are vol · R), with L_g the Laplacian grounded at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the vertex of largest degree and eliminated as for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"numberOfSpanningTrees"},{"type":"text","text":". Every term is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sum of positive ones and the difference loses at most a factor n, so the result keeps its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"relative accuracy under any weight spread. O(n³) time, n² "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The Kemeny constant: the expected number of steps of the random walk (edge weights as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"transition rates, a loop taken with probability 2w\/d(v)) from a vertex to a target drawn"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the stationary distribution, which does not depend on the start; Σ_{i≥2} 1\/μᵢ over the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"normalized Laplacian spectrum. nil when the graph is not connected, 0 for zero or one vertex."}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/Spectra